# ocr-lens.config: operational knobs for the OCR (open-code-review) cross-model review lens.
#
# The gateways (endpoint, model, key source, extra request body) are the review plugin's
# ocr_gateways setting, a JSON array read by scripts/ocr-lens.sh; see the /ocr-lens skill.
# This file holds only the caps. It is sourced by bash; keep it to assign-if-unset lines and
# comments, so a pre-set environment variable wins for a one-off run.

: "${OCR_USE_ANTHROPIC:=false}"

# Max tool-call rounds per file. `--max-tools` can only RAISE ocr's per-file budget above its
# review template default (about 30); a value below it is a no-op, so it cannot cap exploration
# downward. The real per-review bounds are the token budget and the wall-clock cap below (and a
# gateway's extra body that turns reasoning output off, which is what stops a reasoning-loop
# hang). 0 = template default; raise it only for very large files that need more rounds.
: "${OCR_LENS_MAX_TOOLS:=0}"
# Hard token cap per review (a cost guard); ocr publishes partial results and exits 0 if hit.
: "${OCR_LENS_TOKEN_BUDGET:=400000}"
# Wall-clock cap (seconds) for one whole multi-file review before the lens degrades to FAILED.
# Size it so the token budget, not the clock, is the binding cap: a short timeout mislabels a
# slow but progressing run as FAILED. To make the lens faster, lower OCR_LENS_TOKEN_BUDGET.
: "${OCR_LENS_TIMEOUT:=2400}"

# The ocr version this lens is tested against (install with
# `npm install -g @alibaba-group/open-code-review@<version>`).
: "${OCR_LENS_VERSION:=1.8.6}"
